"""Error codes extracted from the Go implementation. DO NOT EDIT BY HAND.

Regenerate with ``python server/scripts/extract_error_codes.py``. The Go sources
(pkg/models/error.go, pkg/user/error.go) are the source of truth.

Keys are "<source>.<GoErrorType>", e.g. "models.ErrProjectDoesNotExist". Neither
the code value nor the constant name is unique upstream:

* codes 1022, 1025 and 1026 are each shared by two errors in pkg/user/error.go;
* code 6002 is shared by ErrTeamDoesNotExist and ErrExternalTeamDoesNotExist
  (pkg/models/error.go declares ErrCodeOIDCTeamDoesNotExist = 6008 but never
  returns it — copied as-is, we return 6002 like the Go version does);
* the type name ErrInvalidTimezone exists in both files with different codes
  (models 2003, user 1025).

Keying by anything less specific would silently drop errors.
"""

